invariant: INV-17
file: ghash_hw.c
catches: ghash_equiv_test
reason: the AES=hw GHASH state holds the pass's sums after the powers of
  H, past the end of the wipe, which covers the state up to the last
  power the call computed. So the carry-less products of the last pass's
  blocks and powers of H stay in the dead frame after every call, and a
  later caller's uninitialized stack reads them. No output changes, so no
  vector notices. bin/ghash_equiv_test copies the stack below one call over
  three passes and requires none of the last pass's three sums in the
  copy.

--- old
    ghash_sums sums;     // the products a multiply or a pass adds up, before reduce
    ghash_vector powers[GHASH_PASS_BLOCKS]; // powers[i] holds H^(i + 1) * x^-1
--- new
    ghash_vector powers[GHASH_PASS_BLOCKS]; // powers[i] holds H^(i + 1) * x^-1
    ghash_sums sums;     // the products a multiply or a pass adds up, before reduce
